Now bump-phone edits. Need careful modify walkPass with jump flag, and backToSales detect Karrot home.

Implement in walkPass:
```
let restart = false;
...
if (done === "bump") { reread=true; break; }
```
For any handled pending item, window closed. But existing logic only restart on bump because price editing may not reset list? priceOne also backToSales closing windows maybe list resets. Tests? Focus. For cooldown skip existing done skip. We should set restart after any done that isn't gone? But some skips occur without window (reserved etc) and don't close. For cooldown skip bumpOne opens and closes. done "skip" indistinguishable from other skips (priceOne skip). But in loop, after priceOne skip also backToSales. For safety set `restart = true` for any done === "bump" || done === "skip" (successful handled path) and break, rather than continue stale cards. But existing test might expect processing multiple cards in one screen? Could increase swipes but okay. However skip due alreadyApplied occurs before calling bumpOne and continues; those don't set. Only after actual action. That may be intended.

But current logic for bump sets reread true and continue same turn without positioning, relying list top. We'll replace with single bottom move. Variable maybe `jumpBottom`. At bottom of loop:
```
if (restart) {
  swipeList(serial, exec, ops, "창을 닫고 목록이 맨 위로 돌아가서", "bottom");
  prev = "";
  stuck = 0;
  page = 0;
  continue;
}
```
But note `reread` existing for gone. Keep.

Maybe after bump item close, if list didn't reset (not top) jumping bottom still valid because walking bottom-up. Good.

Set restart only done bump/skip/price? For done price also window closed, list may reset. Do all non-gone.

But a skip could be because window didn't open, backToSales maybe no-op and list stays at current. Jumping bottom then walking again could cause extra swipes but still eventually. Test "진전이 없으면" no taps (article missing) no action. Fine.

Could minimize by only set restart for `done === "bump" || done === "skip"` all. Let's patch.

backToSales: add home detection. Keep loop. At top for each iteration, get xml. If sales return. If discard... else if karrot home -> openSales and then if sales return else continue. But openSales itself dumps and deep-links. Use `karrotHome(xml)` check. Also if current screen not karrot at all (kakao) and not sales -> maybe openSales too rather than back. Test wants not leave app. After home reopened, fine. What if on menu/sheet not sales (karrot package) - back. Define karrotHome specifically.

Order: home check before back. Add after discard block:
```
if (karrotHome(xml)) { openSales(serial, exec); if (onSales(dumpXml(serial,exec))) return; continue; }
```
But openSales dumps cached? dumpXml after show. It acts. In test deep link sets mode list top0. Good. Maybe calling openSales inside backToSales okay.

Need avoid repeated back falling to kakao if openSales fails. openSales only one attempt. Fine.

Define:
```
function karrotHome(xml:string): boolean {
 return xml.includes("com.towneers.www") && xml.includes("나의 당근") && !onSales(xml);
}
```

Patch.

